  "content": {
    "id": "p44-q51-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "51",
    "prompt": "Let the roots of $x^4+4x^3-2x^2-3x+1=0$ be $\\alpha$, $\\beta$, $\\gamma$ and $\\delta$. Find the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p44-q51-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma+\\delta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-4$",
          "worked": "$$\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma+\\delta=-\\frac41=-4.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q51-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2+\\delta^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$20$",
          "worked": "The sum of products of roots in pairs is $-2$. Write $S=\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma+\\delta$ and $E=\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\alpha\\delta+\\beta\\gamma+\\beta\\delta+\\gamma\\delta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2+\\delta^2&=S^2-2E\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2+\\delta^2&=(-4)^2-2(-2)\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2+\\delta^2&=20.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q51-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1\\alpha+\\dfrac1\\beta+\\dfrac1\\gamma+\\dfrac1\\delta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3$",
          "worked": "The sum of products in triplets is $3$, and the product of all four roots is $1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta+\\frac1\\gamma+\\frac1\\delta&=\\frac{\\alpha\\beta\\gamma+\\alpha\\beta\\delta+\\alpha\\gamma\\delta+\\beta\\gamma\\delta}{\\alpha\\beta\\gamma\\delta}\\\\\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta+\\frac1\\gamma+\\frac1\\delta&=\\frac31\\\\\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta+\\frac1\\gamma+\\frac1\\delta&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q51-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1{\\alpha^2}+\\dfrac1{\\beta^2}+\\dfrac1{\\gamma^2}+\\dfrac1{\\delta^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$13$",
          "worked": "Write $A=\\frac{1}{\\alpha}$, $B=\\frac{1}{\\beta}$, $C=\\frac{1}{\\gamma}$ and $D=\\frac{1}{\\delta}$. From part (c), $A+B+C+D=3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}AB+AC+AD+BC+BD+CD&=\\frac{\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\alpha\\delta+\\beta\\gamma+\\beta\\delta+\\gamma\\delta}{\\alpha\\beta\\gamma\\delta}\\\\AB+AC+AD+BC+BD+CD&=-2.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}A^2+B^2+C^2+D^2&=(A+B+C+D)^2-2(AB+AC+AD+BC+BD+CD)\\\\A^2+B^2+C^2+D^2&=3^2-2(-2)\\\\A^2+B^2+C^2+D^2&=13.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q51-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha^3+\\beta^3+\\gamma^3+\\delta^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p44-q51-e-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-79",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p44-q51-e-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Substitute each root, divide by that root and add the four equations.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For any root $r$, divide its quartic equation by $r$:\n$$r^3+4r^2-2r-3+\\frac1r=0.$$\nLet $S_j=\\alpha^j+\\beta^j+\\gamma^j+\\delta^j$. Adding the four equations gives\n$$S_3+4S_2-2S_1-12+\\left(\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta+\\frac1\\gamma+\\frac1\\delta\\right)=0.$$\nUsing parts (a), (b) and (c),\n$$\\begin{align*}S_3+4(20)-2(-4)-12+3&=0\\\\S_3&=-79.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q51-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha^4+\\beta^4+\\gamma^4+\\delta^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p44-q51-f-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "340",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p44-q51-f-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the four original root-substitution equations and use the preceding power sums.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $S_j=\\alpha^j+\\beta^j+\\gamma^j+\\delta^j$. Substitute each root into the quartic and add the four equations:\n$$S_4+4S_3-2S_2-3S_1+4=0.$$\nUsing the previous parts,\n$$\\begin{align*}S_4+4(-79)-2(20)-3(-4)+4&=0\\\\S_4&=340.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
